{
  "dom_id": "step-q63862",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that a geometric sequence has the first term ${a}_{1}=5$, the common ratio $r=2$, and the $n$th term ${a}_{n}=160$, what is the value of $n?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the index, we substitute our known values of ${a}_{1}$, $r$ and ${a}_{n}$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\ 160 & =5\\cdot {2}^{n-1} \\\\ \\frac{160}{5} & ={2}^{n-1} \\\\ 32 & ={2}^{n-1} \\\\ {2}^{5} & ={2}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the exponents gives:\n\n$$\n5=n-1\\,⟹\\,n=6\n$$\n\nWe can check this result by substituting $n=6$ into the formula for the $n$th term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{n-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {2}^{6-1} \\\\  & =5\\cdot {2}^{5} \\\\  & =5\\cdot 32 \\\\  & =160\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$",
